Spec: Weld Text/Shapes

Purpose:
  Merge overlapping shapes along their boundaries, removing internal lines
  where shapes touch. Essential for laser-cutting text where letters overlap.

Owns:
  ./weld.ts
  ./weld.test.ts

Must:
  Weld is a union that also removes overlapping internal segments.
  Work on 2+ selected closed paths.
  Produce a single closed path as output.
  Preserve the outermost contour only.
  Be fully undoable (restore all original shapes on undo).
  Notify user if weld produces no result (non-overlapping shapes).

Must not:
  Leave internal cut lines between welded shapes.
  Work on open paths (require closed paths).
  Modify unselected shapes.

Depends on:
  paper.js (unite operation)
  @IShape
  @useStore
  @notify

Scenario: weld overlapping letters
  Given text "LR" has been converted to paths with overlapping serifs
  When the user selects all letter paths and clicks "Weld"
  Then a single outline path replaces all letter paths
  And no internal lines remain where letters overlapped

Scenario: weld non-overlapping shapes
  Given two separate circles with no overlap are selected
  When the user clicks "Weld"
  Then a notification says "Shapes do not overlap — weld produces no change"
  And original shapes are preserved

Tasks:
  [ ] Create WeldCommand class (similar to BooleanCommand but focused on union + cleanup).
  [ ] Implement weld logic using Paper.js unite.
  [ ] Remove internal paths from result (keep only outer contour).
  [ ] Add "Weld" button to Properties panel operations section.
  [ ] Add keyboard shortcut (Ctrl+W).
  [ ] Add unit tests for overlapping shapes.
  [ ] Add unit tests for non-overlapping shapes.
  [ ] Add user notification on empty result.

Done when:
  Overlapping closed paths merge into a single outer contour.
  Internal segments between touching shapes are removed.
  Undo restores all original shapes.
  Non-overlapping shapes produce a warning notification.
